{
  "answer": "The Grotesque Tree is a close-range ambush threat with ugly reach and a nasty control package: it has AC 11, 39 HP, 600-foot blindsight, and is vulnerable to fire. Its branch attack reaches 60 feet, and if it lands a hit it can snare the target, grappling and suspending them 20 feet up; it can hold two grappled creatures and later sling them 60 feet for bludgeoning damage. It also resists bludgeoning, ignores piercing, and is immune to charm, so it\u2019s not a straightforward brute-force fight.\n\nFor GM handling, it\u2019s meant to attack anything within 30 feet and retaliate against ranged attacks, usually focusing the nearest enemy until the immediate threat is gone. That makes the fight feel less like a stationary boss and more like a punishing area-denial hazard, especially if the party clusters or opens with bows.\n\nThe site itself is the garden area of The Grotesque Tree, nested in The Jove\u2019s Home, and the module callout says the bark looks armor-tough, the branches are thick with thorns, and there\u2019s a magical aura with roots beneath the village. It also flags shiny metal leaves on odd branches at Passive Perception 15, arcane infusion at Arcana 12/17, and treasure in the form of precious metal leaves worth 100 gp after the fight.",
  "envelope_revision_id": "rev:4996a37341f4dd9a9e536c2aa0263d41",
